  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: cbc795acf92c1fb48bae236e4ba4d39f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q08_Bias_Reverse
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::PNJunctionLab.AssessmentQuestion
  questionId: q08_rev_bias
  topic: 3
  topicTag: 4. Forward & Reverse Bias
  shortSummaryLabel: Reverse Bias & Is Leakage
  promptText: Connecting + to the N terminal and - to P applies reverse bias (V = -VR < 0, below breakdown). What occurs?
  options:
  - Barrier rises to V0 + VR, W widens, blocking majority carriers; tiny minority leakage Is flows
  - Depletion width shrinks to zero and illuminates a series indicator LED
  - Majority holes pour rapidly across the junction from P to N
  - Reverse saturation current Is drops to zero when temperature rises
  correctIndex: 0
  explanation: Reverse bias reinforces the internal barrier (V0 + VR) and widens W, suppressing majority diffusion while allowing only tiny thermally generated minority leakage Is (which rises with T).
  recommendedStation: Station 5
